<title>UK: BA January load factor rises 0.9 points.</title>
<headline>BA January load factor rises 0.9 points.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Airways Plc said on Wednesday scheduled revenue passenger kilometres rose 9 percent in January on the previous year. Seat capacity rose by 7.6 percent, giving a scheduled passenger load factor of 67.5 percent, up 0.9 percentage points on last year.</p>
<p>Cargo tonne kilometres rose 9.7 percent over January last year.</p>
</text>
